N.50="comment"*26x54*80x33
C="{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\deff0\\deflang1033{\\fonttbl{\\f0\\fswiss\\fprq2\\fcharset0 Calibri;}{\\f1\\fnil\\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\\colortbl ;\\red31\\green73\\blue125;}
\\viewkind4\\uc1\\pard\\cf1\\f0\\fs22 I would compile it once targeted for the f280x to make sure it compiles OK.\\par
If you don\\rquote t\\rquote  want the hotlink, then don\\rquote t check the \\ldblquote\\cf0 Include VisSim Communication\\cf1\\rdblquote  option\\par
\\cf0\\par
Target = Generic MCU\\par
Use selected edge pins CHECKED (otherwise it will generate code for the entire model, debug CB's as well, and the ndk will error)\\par
Call from Foreign RTOS CHECKED\\par
\\par
Edit c source file and comment out all lines containing \"hotlink\"\\f1\\fs18\\par
}
"
N.51="comment"*40x33*101x28<M>
C="{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\deff0\\deflang1033{\\fonttbl{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\\colortbl ;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;}
\\viewkind4\\uc1\\pard\\fs18 Production Version:  DO NOT INCLUDE THE DEBUG OUTPUT  COMPOUND BLOCKS (BELOW)  IN THE CODEGEN (another copy is included in the level above)\\par
\\par
Debug Version:  Include this entire block  OR the desired \"Debug Outputs\" (shown as compound blocks below) in the codegen block, filter the Android monitor output on \"Ric\".  NOTE:  the \"Debug Outputs\" are ordered alphabetically from \"Ric0\" to \"Ric1\" to \"Ric2\",...\\par
\\par
\\cf1\\fs16 Line Break Ric0 occurs before Ric1 occurs before Ric2 before Ric3...\\par
\\par
NOTE:  %f format will not output values < 0\\par
\\cf0\\fs18\\par
}
"
