N.392="comment"*126x68*120x15
C="{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\deff0\\deflang1033{\\fonttbl{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0 Arial;}{\\f1\\froman\\fprq2\\fcharset0 Liberation Serif;}{\\f2\\froman\\fprq2\\fcharset0 Arial;}{\\f3\\froman\\fprq2\\fcharset0 Calibri;}{\\f4\\froman\\fprq2\\fcharset2 Symbol;}{\\f5\\fswiss\\fprq2\\fcharset0 Calibri;}{\\f6\\fswiss\\fprq2\\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\\colortbl ;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;}
\\viewkind4\\uc1\\pard\\fs20 v139 - 1/24/24\\par
1.  changed heating criteria; if temp1 > temp2 + 6 deg once, latch to heating mode, if temp1 < temp 2 - 6 deg, latch to cooling mode.  SAT = temp 1, RAT = temp 2\\par
2. Ch1 AppType control the Apptype for the node, all other CH AppTypes are ignored\\par
3.  cycles per hour limiter and native time delay functions are not active\\par
4. Heat pump on time boost while heating is not present (90 sec on)\\par
5. Master slave logic removed \\par
6.  Cooling control is from v138 with no changes\\par
\\par
\\par
v138 - 10/10/23\\par
1. Added hard limits on SAT max and min\\par
2. Simplified the SAT and RAT max and min calculations\\par
3. Removed midnight logic, the algorithm resets at midnight every day, no memory values are saved\\par
\\par
v137 - 10/7/23\\par
1.  Removed the precommissioning logic and added RLS to the 30 min commissioning, lamda is in Constants.  Response is must faster and more accurate.  \\par
\\par
v136 - 10/4/23\\par
1.  Changed RAT MAX1 from .4 to .15 degF and MAX2 from 2 to .3 degF for more accurate RAT control.\\par
2.  Turned off Pre Commissioning logic and running the 30 min only commissioning.  This had better setpoint results\\par
3.  Issue1: when communication is lost, the algorithm continues to operate in whatever state it was in normally, when communication is restored, the pace starts online, should start in bypass.  Tom W is testing what the pace relay does when communication is lost and restored on his desktop device.  \\par
Issue2:  everytime an OTA is done, if the pace is bypassed prior to the OTA, it goes online for 1-2 minutes, then goes to bypass.  if the pace is online prior to the OTA, it goes online and remains online after the OTA.  It should go to bypass after an OTA.  \\par
An OTA is a soft reset which means that the powerUpFlag is set for an OTA and for the midnight soft reset. \\par
Addition:  if dayTime < 24hr - delta, and powerupflag signal, then this is a OTA, close all relays for 5 min. \\par
\\par
\\par
v135 - 9/29/23:\\par
1.  Corrected bypass signal, I had left logic that controlled the bypass\\par
2.  Set forgetting factor = .9997 (was .999997)\\par
\\par
\\par
v134 - 9/28/23\\par
1.  Corrected tOff not connected in cycler (this was an error in v133)\\par
2.  Set RLS to reinitialize when commishRE\\par
3.  Modified the SAT RAT controller tOn conditions to put more emphasis on the RAT error\\par
4.  Lowered the High RAT to 2 deg instead of 3deg.\\par
\\par
\\par
v133 - 9/22/23\\par
1.  Oversized Equipment logic addition:  Added \"Oversized Equipment Logic\" CB top level, this block measures the longest ON time and the responsible channel number.  When the ON time falls below \"OVERSIZED MIN ONTIME\" (set to 240 sec), it then sets a global flag \"isDecimateGBL\" which remains on for \"DECIMATE TIME DURATION\" (set to 2 hours), then the logic is re-evaluated.  Each channel controller CB includes a \"Decimate\" CB to process the uOEM signal.  The \"Decimate\" block creates a new uOEM signal for that channel with every \"OEM PULSE TO DECIMATE\" (set to 4) removed.  \\par
\\par
v132 - 9/14/23\\par
1. Removed the v131 logic that added 90 second debounce\\par
2. \\cf1\\fs19 Added logic to commissioning to prevent isOnline from cycling during the midnight reset.  This logic is based on the secondsPastMidnightGBL timer value which is reset to 0 at midnight.  Then from 10 minutes before midnight the isOnline state is prevented from changing until 10 minutes after midnight. The RE and FE signals are set to 0 for this time as well.  \\par
\\par
\\cf0\\fs20 v131 - 9/13/23\\par
1.  Added 90 second debounce to the bypass command to prevent the unit from cycling from online to bypass then back to online during the midnight soft reset.  Tom W estimated the reset time to be betwee 55 seconds to 75 seconds so the 90 second debounce should take care of this. \\par
\\par
v130 - 9/6/23\\line 1.  decreased tOnmin to 300 seconds (was 372 seconds)\\par
2.  Increased the RAT delta to 3 deg (was 0.8 deg)\\par
\\par
v129 - 9/5/23\\par
1.  changed tOnmax = 1800 instead of 3600\\par
2.  cutout logic to release control to OEM if abs(SAT - RAT) < 3 deg for 3600 sec\\par
3.  tuned tOn min and tOff min limit logic in cycler to make it more robust\\par
\\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 v128 - 9/1/23\\par
1. Replaced the RAT SAT Controller triggering (based on uOEMRE or PaceRE) and feedhack gain based on SAT and RAT error with timer based triggering (triggers every 600 seconds) and a fixed increase or decrease time based on SAT and RAT error.\\par
\\par
2.  Commissioning - now both the precommissioning and 30 min commissioning run. If the precommission SAT max, min, RAT max, min RLS are not calculated, then the 30 min values are used.\\par
\\par
3.  Reworked the Anti Short Cycle Logic\\par
\\par
v127 - 8/20/23\\par
1. Removed the short ON time protection and only left in the short OFF time protection\\par
2.  Removed all extended commissioning logic because the pre commissioning should take care of it\\par
3.  Removed the relay close at midnight\\par
\\par
V126 - 8/29/23\\par
1.  Changed RLS commissioning time from 48 hours to 1 hours (3600 sec)\\par
2.  Corrected \\ldblquote FE + SAT Max Logic\\rdblquote  and \\ldblquote RE + SAT Min Logic\\rdblquote  in \\ldblquote SAT and RAT Precommissioning, the SAT max calculation did not include \\ldblquote > SAT MIN LIMIT\\rdblquote  and the  SAT min calculation did not include \\ldblquote < SAT MAX LIMIT\\rdblquote .  This resulted in SAT min values being much larger than SAT max values.\\par
\\pard 3. removed \\ldblquote isSATLowGBL\\rdblquote  and \\ldblquote isRATLowGBL\\rdblquote  and associated logic in the cyclers\\kerning0\\f0\\fs20\\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 V124 - 8/21/23\\par
1.  tOnMax = 372 sec\\par
2.  Set  \\ldblquote isSATLowGBL\\rdblquote  and \\ldblquote isRATLowGBL\\rdblquote  = 0 to prevent the Low SAT and Low RAT logic from operating in the cycler.\\par
3.  Replace the 30min commissioning period with 2 day pre-commissioning that uses the RLS estimator to estimate the SATmin, SATmax, RATmin, and RATmax.  COMMISH_TIME set to 2 days instead of 1800 sec.  Added a variable in the \\ldblquote Constants\\rdblquote  CB to switch between the 30 min and 2 day commissioning.\\par
\\pard 4.  Modified the RLS to stop computing the covariance and RLS once commissioning completed (worried about over/underflow).\\kerning0\\f0\\fs20\\par
\\par
\\par
v123 - 8/19/23 - MAKING WAVES ONLY\\par
1. tOnmax = 180 sec instead of 270 sec\\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 2.  Added 2 Delta Temperature constants when the RAT or SAT is below the setpoint,\\par
DELTA RAT BELOW SETPOINT = .2 \\par
DELTA SAT BELOW SETPOINT = .5\\par
These values are used in the SAT and RAT Measurement blocks \\ldblquote SAT MAX Value and SAT States\\rdblquote  and RAT MAX Value and RAT States\\rdblquote  to create the variables \\ldblquote isSATLowGBL\\rdblquote  and \\ldblquote isRATLowGBL\\rdblquote .  These variables are created using hysteresis to prevent chattering.    These variables are applied to the last calculation in the \\ldblquote Cycler\\rdblquote  to open the relay if \\ldblquote isOnlineAFterCommish\\rdblquote  AND \\ldblquote isRATLowGBL\\rdblquote  AND \\ldblquote isSATLowGBL\\rdblquote  is true.  Once the condition is set to false, normal tOn cycling occurs.  \\par
\\par
\\pard 3.  Corrected SAT State and RAT State calculations to use \\ldblquote SAT Maximum Value\\rdblquote  instead of \\ldblquote SATSensorValue\\rdblquote  and RAT Maximum Value\\rdblquote  instead of \\ldblquote RATSensorValue\\rdblquote .  There was excessive cycling between the states before this change was made because all values and not just the Max values were being compared with the commish Max value.  \\par
\\kerning0\\f0\\fs20\\par
\\par
v122 - 8/16/23- MAKING WAVES ONLY\\par
1.  \\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 Modification to commissioning state 1 (no compressor on during commissioning).  The problem is the SAT estimator runs for the entire commissioning and while no compressors are running the SAT max and RAT max values are too high.  A change was added to the SAT and RAT estimators to begin commissioning after 1 complete compressor cycle has occurred.  \\par
\\par
2.  SAT and RAT preprocessing (within SAT and RAT Measurements CB) to collect SAT and RAT values and take an average \\par
\\par
3.  tOnmax = 270 sec instead of 372 sec\\kerning0\\f0\\fs20\\par
\\par
v121 - 8/14/23\\par
1. reworked the extended commissioning profile logic so it only created one off cycle of 192 seconds then closed the relay for the duration of the extended commissioning timerange (1800 sec is the time range, this means for the next 1608 seconds the relay is closed)\\par
\\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1\\f2 V120 - 8/13/23\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 1.  increased ON TIME GAIN DECREASE from .8 to .9 to maintain larger values of tOn right after commissioning.  The .9 reduced the on time by 60 seconds on the first iteration after commissioning and caused SAT to increase too rapidily to be controlled.\\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1 2.  Changed DELTA SAT MAX1 from 2 deg to .25 degF, Changed DELTA SAT MAX2 LOW LOAD from 3 deg to .5 deg, changed  DELTA SAT MAX2 HIGH LOAD from 2.5 deg to .5 deg.\\kerning0\\f2\\fs20\\par
\\pard\\f0\\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1\\f2 v119 - 8/11/23\\par
1.  complete rework of extended commissioning logic.  This is only used if there are no OEM cycles during the normal commissioning period which would not produce controllable SAT and RAT min and max values. If there is at least one RE and FE OEM signal during normal commissioning, the extended commissioning logic is not used. Tested on 10 data files with results in \"V119TestCases.xls\".  Four different commissioning states are defined; normal, all compressors OFF, at least one compressor full on, and not enough OEM RE and FE to get SAT and RAT min and max values. Four constants defining the commissioning states were added.  A .1 deg tolerance was included for the profile generator pulldown error from RAT setpoint.  A profile generator was implemented using a state machine in the commissioning block.  Changes were also made to the cyclers/ Short ON & OFF Cycle protection CB. Also the Find Lead Compressor During Commissioning CB was simplified to only calcualte the lead compressor number.  All other sorting was removed.   \\par
2.  changed tOn min from 300 sec to 372 seconds (for high OAT in Texas)  \\par
\\par
v118 - 8/8/23\\par
Identical to v117, no changes made, think Tom W may have ota'd a corrupted file\\par
\\par
v117 - 8/7/23\\par
\\pard\\cf1\\f0\\fs19 Special Commissioning Logic:  If the commissioning time has been exceeded (30 min) AND if the OEMRE count = 0 OR the OEMFE count = 0, \\par
then set \"applySpecialCaseCommissioning\" flag ON.  While this flag is ON, the \"Profile to cycle the full on compressor\" block is executed. \\par
This block creates 5 on-off cycles applied to the compressor with the longest ON time during commissioning.  \\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1\\cf0\\f2\\fs20\\par
\\par
V116 - 8/5/23\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\f2\\fs20 1.  3 degree logic cutout timer trigger changed to react to both RE and FE of the input signal (the input signal is the boolean of abs(SAT-RAT) < 3 deg.  Originally this was set to RE only and this caused the three degree cutout flag to remain ON when it should have been Off.\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\f2\\fs20 2.  3 degree logic into FF, added RE to the \\lquote threeDegDCutout\\rdblquote  set input and  removed the \\ldblquote not uOEM\\rdblquote  condition from the reset input of the FF.  \\f3\\fs22\\par
\\f2\\fs20 3. RAT SAT Control, OR\\rquote d isBpyassedThisChannel with isCommishFE to initialize tOn after a bypass occurs. \\f3\\fs22\\par
\\f2\\fs20 4.  increased tOnMax from 1800 to 3600 sec.\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\f2\\fs20 5.  end of commissioning condition modified to be > 1800 sec AND at least 4 OEM RE and 4 OEM FE signals.\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\f2\\fs20 6.  SAT and RAT commish values modified to occur from >1 OEM RE and >1 OEM FE signal to the end of commissioning.  \\par
\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24\\par
\\par
V115 - 8/3/23\\par
1.  SAT Logic and Measurements:  Replaced \\ldblquote SAT Maximum Value GBL\\rdblquote  with \\ldblquote SAT Sensor Value GBL\\rdblquote  in the three flag values; \\ldblquote isSATNormalGBL\\rdblquote , \\ldblquote isSATSlightlyHighGBL\\rdblquote , and \\ldblquote isSATVeryHighGBL\\rdblquote\\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1 2.  RAT Logic and Measurements:  Replaced \\ldblquote RAT Maximum Value GBL\\rdblquote  with \\ldblquote RAT Sensor Value GBL\\rdblquote  in the three flag values; \\ldblquote isRATNormalGBL\\rdblquote , \\ldblquote isRATSlightlyHighGBL\\rdblquote , and \\ldblquote isRATVeryHighGBL\\rdblquote\\par
\\pard\\kerning0\\f0\\fs20\\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 v114 - 8/2/23\\par
\\pard\\fi-360\\li720\\kerning2\\f4\\fs22\\'b7\\tab\\f5 Added tOffMax value = 300 sec to RAT SAT Controller\\par
*     Reduced ON TIME MAS from 3600 to 1800\\par
\\f4\\'b7\\tab\\f5 Modified how tOn increases. it now increases at every uOEMRE or every pace RE.  This logic only works if NOT commish, during commish no increase in tOn is allowed. \\par
*      REduced the tOn gain from .9 to .8\\par
*      Replaced the tOn gain of 1 with a gain of 1.075 for slight violations of temperature.\\par
\\f4\\'b7\\tab\\f5 Added IsCommish OR\\rquote d with seconds past midnight to keep the relay closed in this state, else it allowed the protected value to come through, in the Cycler Short ON and OFF Protection circuit. Also remove the debounce and added AND with uOEM to the input.  \\par
\\f4\\'b7\\tab\\f5 Removed all lag and lead logic from cyclers \\par
\\pard\\kerning0\\f0\\fs20\\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 v113 - 7/24/23\\par
1.  Modified the tOn logic in the RAT SAT controller to prevent sampling at both an OEMRE and a PaceRE, without this change the tOn signal increased and decreased too rapidly.  \\par
\\par
v112 - 7/22/23\\par
1. Changed the commish logic so that  commissioning could be turned off for a short (4 min) online command.  This prevents commissioning from never turning off when the online command is < 1800 sec (which causes the relays to remain closed forever regardless of there  being another offline-online cycle)\\par
\\par
\\par
v111 - 7/21/23\\par
1.  Corrected the SAT Min, Max and RAT Min, Max logic.  The problem situation was the Min or Max logic could output a 0.  Added continuous sampling to reset the \"min\" and \"max\" compares if this situation occured.  This assumes the SAT and RAT sensor values are valid. \\par
2.  Corrected the SATMAX DELTA value, it was always being calculated as the high load case, now it calculates the DELTA for both high and low loads correctly. \\par
\\par
V110 - 7/19/23\\kerning0\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 1.  Modified RAT SAT controllers to increase and decrease tOn, logic was simplified also\\kerning0\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 2.  Removed AND OEM from cycler, now the pace relays will close when there is no OEM signal and offline-online\\kerning0\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 3.  Reduced RAT temperature limits from .5 and 1 to .4 and .8\\kerning0\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 4.  Reduced SAT temperature limits from 2 and 4 to 2 and 3\\par
\\par
V109 - 7/17/23\\kerning0\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 1.  added 3 sec debounce  to the input to the cycler/ short ON & OFF Cycle Protect.\\kerning0\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 2.  Reduced ON TIME MAX from 7200 to 840 seconds. The 2W machine can do a pulldown in two  minutes so there is no need for such a large value.\\kerning0\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\pard\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 3. Removed the tOnMAX limit from the tOn calculation in the RAT SAT Controller.  An upper limit on tOn is not needed.\\kerning0\\f0\\fs20\\par
\\par
v107 - 7/14/23:\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 1. In each cycler, after the pace relay command has been created, the following logic is added in the block \\ldblquote Relay Open Check\\rdblquote ;\\par
\\cf1\\f6\\fs19 If 2 or more OEM channels are ON and at least 2 of the ON channel Pace relays are closed,\\cf0\\f1\\fs24\\par
\\cf1\\f6\\fs19 OR if 1 or less OEM channels are ON regardless of their Pace relay state, then it is ok to \\cf0\\f1\\fs24\\par
\\cf1\\f6\\fs19  allow this channel control to open the Pace relay.  \\par
Otherwise,this channel may not open its relay until the isOKToTurnThisChannelOff flag goes to 1.\\cf0\\f1\\fs24\\par
\\par
\\cf1\\f6\\fs19 2.  In the SAT MAX Measurement block/ added the following logic block \\ldblquote High Temp Reset\\rdblquote  to account  for high load condition where channels are on continuously causing SAT MIN ~= SAT MAX.    If the increased value is required\\cf0\\f1\\fs24\\par
\\cf1\\f6\\fs19 at any time during a day, it will remain in effect until midnight when it is reset\\cf0\\f1\\fs24\\par
\\pard\\cf1\\f6\\fs19 to the normal value\\cf0\\kerning0\\f0\\fs20\\par
\\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 V106 - 7/13/23\\par
1.  Commissioning/ removed \\ldblquote channelOnCount > 0\\rdblquote  from the FF \\ldblquote Set\\rdblquote  logic, now the commissioning FF is set when isOnline = 1\\par
2.  SAT RAT Control/ Added 2 sec delay to uOEM vector in SAT RAT controller to synchronize with the measured On time.\\par
3.  SAT RAT Control/ Modified the logic to reset tOn.  When commishFE occurs, tOn is initialized to the uOEM ontime during previous uOEM cycle, this time is calculated at uOEMFE.  When either the SAT or RAT gets very high, tOn is initialized to the ON TIME MAX (7200 sec) to give the OEM control time to get the temperatures back to normal.\\par
\\par
V105 - 7/11/23\\par
1.  Removed uOEMCycleCountGBL from each cycler and replaced with uOEMRE\\par
2.  Removed uOEMCycleCountGBL from \\ldblquote Measure OEM OnTime, OffTime\\rdblquote\\par
3.  Removed \\ldblquote Commish Pulse\\rdblquote  from \\ldblquote Measure OEM OnTime, OffTime\\rdblquote\\par
4. Modified the \"Measure OEM OnTime, OffTime\" to record normal OEM On and Off times and On and Off times during commissioning.\\par
5.  \\ldblquote Cycler\\rdblquote  close relay if not a lag channel\\par
6. SAT RAT Controller: removed delays from tOn and tOff to eliminate single second relay open states.\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1 7.  \\ldblquote Cycler\\rdblquote  moved \\ldblquote Short On and OFF cycle Protect\\rdblquote  further upstream to not affect the \\ldblquote relay close\\rdblquote  state from commissioning or not being the lag channel.  \\par
8. Did not completely fix the situation where ch1 and ch2 are wired together.\\par
\\kerning0\\f3\\fs22\\par
V104 - 7/9/23\\par
1. Removed the \\ldblquote isOnlineAfterCommishGBL\\rdblquote  NOT signal from the FF used to start commissioning.  This will allow commissioning to occur whenevre the \\ldblquote isOnlineGBL\\rdblquote  value is cycled.  \\par
\\pard\\f0\\fs20\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 V103 -7/8/23\\par
1.  cyclers: corrected SAT and RAT high and very high logic, it was not correct. \\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1 2.  in 568, commish occurred at launch and not at 60000+ sec when it was supposed to, need to add logic to isOnlineGBL and isBypassFromCloudPortalGBL to ignore the first pass, value of these two.   \\kerning0\\f2\\fs20\\par
\\pard\\f0\\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1\\f2 v102 - 7/6/23\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\f2\\fs20 1.  removed SAT control from cycler, the cycler only responds to the tVec values\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\f2\\fs20 2. RAT Controller renamed to controller with two control methods; temperature control and time based control.\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\f2\\fs20 3.  added a commissioning phase which lasts for 30 minutes once at least one compressor turns on.  In this phase all four relays are closed and the OEM controls the unit allowing measurement of the SAT MAX and RAT MAX. This phase will execute when the cloud bypass command is set to 0. \\f3\\fs22\\par
\\f2\\fs20 4. Added logic to detect if ch1 is wired to ch2 (no other channels are checked, only ch1 and ch2)\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\f2\\fs20 5. RAT SAT Controller Operation\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 :\\kerning0\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\li720\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 a.  For a given channel, when commissioning completes, the tOn is set to the most recent OEM On time and the tOff to 192 seconds (3.2 minutes).  \\kerning0\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 b.  At the start of each successive OEM signal, the tOn value is reduced using the equation; tOn = .9*tOn(previous).  \\kerning0\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 c.  If tOn decreases to its lower limit = 270 seconds (4.5 minutes), the tOff value begins to increase using the equation; tOff = 1.075*tOff(previous) until it reaches its upper limit = 300 seconds.  \\kerning0\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\li720\\sl240\\slmult1\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 d.  If tOn is limited and tOff is increasing and if either the SAT or RAT is very high, tOff is reset to its original 192 seconds steps a.-c. are repeated.\\kerning0\\f3\\fs22\\par
\\f2\\fs20\\par
\\pard\\f0 6. added minimum ON and OFF time protection to each cycler\\par
\\par
\\par
v101 - 7/3/23\\par
1.  Added variables for SAT MIN and SAT MAX limiting, changed limits to 50 and 60 respectively. (changes to Constants and SAT Min & Max Measurement CBs)\\par
\\par
2.  Modified logic in \"Prevent additional compressors until SAT completes or SAT time completes\" so that only 1 additional channel comes on when SATRelayCmd goes to 0 (turns off) if the OEM is calling for more compressors.\\par
\\par
\\par
v100 - 7/2/23\\par
1.  Added declaration #include \"android/log.h\" to declare \"ANDROID_LOG_INFO\" which is needed to get the android studio monitor to work. \\par
2. Added 2 offline periods to measure the SAT max and min, one at 1AM, the second at 1PM.  Modifications to the cyclers to go offline (close their relays during these periods).  \\par
3. Protection logic for Sat max and min added, max limited to no less than 60degF, min limited to no less than 54degF, if max-min < 6degF, max = min + 6.\\par
4. maximum offline duration is 1800 sec, maximum wait time for a compressor to come on during an offline period is 3600 sec.\\par
\\par
\\par
\\par
v99 - 6/27/23\\par
1.  Corrected v98, the OFF channels had their relays closed, this is not correct, v99 this was changed by adding the following logic to the SAT controller in each channel. \\par
\\cf1\\fs19 Close Pace relay if (this results in OEM control of the channel)\\par
the Pace is Online AND\\par
if this channel is an active (ON) channel AND\\par
this channel is not the lag channel AND\\par
this channel is not in SAT Control mode\\par
\\cf0\\fs20\\par
v98 - 6/27/23  - DO NOT USE\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\kerning1\\f1\\fs24 1.  added a counter in \\ldblquote Get Lag Channel for Cycler SAT\\rdblquote  to track the number of channels ON\\par
2.  increased the debounce in sortVec from 3 to 15 to avoid data spikes (located in \\ldblquote Get Lag Channel for Cycler SAT\\rdblquote )\\par
3.  Added a timer in \\ldblquote SAT Cooling Control\\rdblquote  to time how long the \\ldblquote SATRelayCmdGBL\\rdblquote  remains ON\\par
\\pard 4.  added a \\ldblquote Prevent addition compressors from coming on \\ldblquote  logic in the \\ldblquote Get Lag Channel for Cycler SAT\\rdblquote using the SAT timer \\kerning0\\f0\\fs20\\par
\\par
V97 - 6/26/23\\par
1. Same as v96 but SAT controller SAT Max set to 63 degF (hardcoded).  \\par
2.  Cleaned up data types for all \"merges\" and lag calculations, added convert blocks throughout\\par
3.  Modified SAT RAT control mode variable to output 0,1,2 instead of 0,1.\\par
\\par
\\par
v96 - 6/22/23\\par
1.  Additional change to cycler to ensure v95 1. works, I don't think it was working in v95\\par
\\par
v95 - 6/22/23\\par
1.  Restrict control to SAT only of the lag channel, all other active channels receive the OEM command\\par
\\par
v94 - 6/21/23\\par
1.  Set SAT Max to 68, SAT Min to 60, both fixed\\par
2.  Added the \"short ON and OFF cycle protect\" function to each of the 5 cyclers.  min ON time set to 4 minutes (240 sec), min OFF time set to 3.2 minutes (192 sec)\\par
3.  Changed most integer constants to \"int\" data type\\par
4.  Brought the \"controlModeVec\" out to the top level for easier viewing\\par
\\par
v93 - 6/19/23\\par
1.  Replaced the SAT Control \"merge\" with 2 ANDs and an OR.  In the 6/19/23 data for 2w, in v92, ch2 should have gone into SAT mode with the relay open but the data collection showed the relay closed.  I think the merge incorrectly was receiving a 0 values boolen instead of 1 as it should be for SAT control. \\par
\\par
v92 - 6/19/23\\par
1. Added time delay to non Lead RAT control channels to prevent non-lead RAT channels from coming on at the same time.  Used a 4 minute delay on each non-lead RAT channel. \\par
\\par
2.  Added 10AM and 2PM RAT setpoint calculations\\par
\\par
3.  Corrected SAT RAT 3 degree logic to only apply when online.   \\par
\\par
\\par
v91 - 6/17/23\\par
1. removed the min On time protection and min off time protection from the cycler downstream of the SAT controller\\par
2. added a debounce (10 seconds) to the output of the cycler.\\par
\\par
v90 - 6/17/23\\par
1.  corrected cycler initialization when SAT controller is ON, keep cycler pacetime = 0\\par
2.  Removed unnecessary code from cyclers (uoemontime, satmax and min) they arre all calculated in a common block at the top level\\par
\\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1\\cf1\\f6\\fs18 v89\\par
1.  improved the SAT min and max estimation, it was missing max estimates if 2 max's occured without a min in between.\\par
2. RAT control logic reverasal corrected, RAT control was incorrectly running on time based control\\par
\\par
v87 - 6/15/23\\par
1.  Removed unused Constants\\par
2.  Moved SAT Cooling Control from each channel to one SAT Cooling Control in the top level of the algorithm.  \\par
3.   Moved Hot Water Heater Control from each channel to one Hot Water Heater Control in the top level of the algorithm.\\par
4.   Moved the 3 degree SAT-RAT logic from each channel to one logic block in the top level of the model.  \\par
5.  Corrected \"loadControllerModeGBL\" definition, it was set to 0 in v86 preventing the SAT logic from working. \\par
6.  SAT Cooling Control only works on the lag compressor instead of all the compressors.\\par
7.  Replaced hysterisis controllers with SR Flip Flops to simplify the algorithm\\par
\\par
v86 - 6/14/23\\par
1.  SAT controller always on for all channels.  The \"sortVecGBL\" vector which ordered the compressors with the lead channel number in element 1 to the lag channel number in the bottommost element.  The \"sortVecGBL\" is used to apply a SAT hysteresis controller offset to the \"turn on\" condition and the \"turn off\" condition.  For the lead compressor, the \"turn on\" offset is set to 2 degF below SAT MAX, for the lead2 compressor the \"turn on\" offset is set to 1.5degF below SAT MAX.  This causes lead 2 to come on only if the SAT continues to increase after the lead compressor turns on.  All the \"turn off\" offsets are set to 1degF greater than the SAT MIN. \\par
\\par
v85 - 6/12/23\\par
1.  Added a 10 second debounce to to the \"Short ON & OFF Cycle Protect\" in the cycler module to prevent impulse inputs from turning on the compressor for the minimum ON time.  This was seen in v84 on channel 3 during the second online period. \\par
V84 - 6/12/23\\par
1.  add \"not(isBypassFromCloudPortalGBL)\" to the \"SAT Control On?\" to prevent SAT control from activating during offline.  When it activates offline an incorrect initial condition is created for the SAT Hysteresis Control logic causing the pace relay to remain closed for the duration of the online period.  \\par
V83 = v82 built using 2023 x64 build 13\\par
\\pard This build produced pace relay results that agreed with the simulation results, v82 which was build using 2020.3 did not agree with the simulation results.  \\cf0\\f0\\fs20\\par
\\par
v82 - 6/10/23\\par
1.  Lag channel calculations modified by ANDing the OEM status (on or off) with the ONtime for that channel.  This was necessary because i saw channels on for 790 seconds, then turn off but the ONtime would hold the last non zero value.  This caused the Lag channel logic to incorrectly identify the correct Lag channel.  \\par
\\par
2.  Increased the upper limit on the SAT Daily Max Value from 65 to 68 degF.  This should allow longer OFF times when under SAT control.  \\par
\\par
3.  RAT Control, RAT Error deadband set to .5 degF.  This reduces the RAT error by 0.5 degF making the RAT controller less responsive to changes in RAT.\\par
\\par
4.  Cyclet/ SAT Logic On CB, corrected the logic to SAT Control On if (lagchNo!=0) AND (lagChNo = this channelNo).  Before, the second part of the AND was (LagchNo!= this channel), this was not correct, want the lag channel to control using the SAT controller and none of the other channels.  \\par
\\par
5.  SAT control, replace SR Flip Flop with logic that does the same thing, I was not sure the FF was calculating correctly.  \\par
\\par
6. Combined all the cycler reset conditions into one CB containing the following OR'd conditions (1) (PaceCycle Time >= Period), (2) uOEMRE, (3) is Bypass FE, (4) is Bypassed, and (5) SAT Control On.  \\par
\\par
7.  Added 2 outputs to the Cycler , SAT Control On and SAT Control, for plotting only, no functional value. \\par
\\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1\\cf1\\f2\\fs18 v81 - 6/10/23\\par
1. increased daily max SAT from 65 to 68, this will provide more off time to the pace cycle\\par
2.  corrected channel numbers, in v80, ch3 was set to ch1 and ch5 to ch2\\par
3.  replaced the SAT controller SR flip flop with a real hysteresis control\\par
\\par
\\par
v80 - 6/9/23\\par
1.  Fixed SAT min and max estimator so it works correctly when Pace is online\\par
2.  Fixed RAT min and max estimator with same logic as SAT\\par
3.  Added deadband to the RAT temperture controller in the load controller\\par
4.  Modified SAT controller to use the newly estimated SAT min and max values\\par
\\par
\\pard v79 - 6/6/23\\par
1.  added SAT control to cycler, pace cycle goes off if SAT is within 1.5 deg of SAT minimum value to prevent undercooling, this should save some energy\\par
2.  fixed SAT min and max estimator, works better now\\par
3.  Added 180 second minimum on and off time with a 10 second debounce to the cycler output to prevent shortcycling, both ON and OFF\\par
4.  changed load control to only RAT control using measured times from historical data.  For the ontime and offtime, a linear equation is used to calculate a factor from the RAT error, then this factor is used to scale the most recent oem on and off times. (the factors are always < 1)\\par
5.  collected all common calculations in single top level blocks\\par
6.  changed 3 degF cutout in cycler to require the 3 degF or less difference between SAT and RAT remain for at least a 30 minute duration instead of a snapshot in time at 30 minutes.  \\par
7.  Added multi compressor lag channel detect in cycler to crate a SAT Contron ON variable, which turns ON when the controlChNoGBL != 1 AND not equal to the individual cycler channel number.\\par
8.  SAT control in cycler: a timer is started when the SAT Control On OR SAT > SATmin+ delta, the relay remains closed until the timer reaches a measured time (this is the time for a pulldown), then it opens.  This is done to prevent undercooling.\\cf0\\f0\\fs20\\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1\\cf1\\f2\\fs18 v78 - 6/2/23\\par
1.  fixed the SAT Max and Min estimator, it was not estimating when the SAT Max decreased, only when it increased\\par
2.  Removed the Load controller and the timer section of the cycler (neither are used in v78) and modified the cycle controller logic to only include a hysteresis control  based on SAT Max and Min.  Pace relay = 0 if SAT <= SAT Min + .5 and Pace relay = 1 if SAT >= SAT Max - .5\\par
\\par
v77 - 5/31/23\\par
1.  Added logic to dynamically order the 5 channels based on the OEM ontime.  Element 1 contains the channel number with the largest on time and Element 5 contains the channel number with the smallest runtime.  \\par
2.  Added logic to each cycler channel to close its relay if it is not the channel with the second largest runtime.  The channel with the largest runtime will remain full on and the cycler will only affect the second largest runtime channel.  \\par
3.  Set tOn to .8*most recent OEM ON time for that channel.  if SAT > SAT Max then the relay is closed until the SAT falls below a measured minimum value.  SAT MAX  and the SAT minimum value are both measured from the most recent SAT data.  tOff set to 180.  \\par
\\pard\\cf0\\f0\\fs20\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1\\cf1\\f2\\fs18 v76 - 5/28/23\\par
1.  Removed RAT Dot logic from load controller and replaced with RAT Error Min (= .5).  If RAT Error Min is less than .5, the tOn will continue to decrease, otherwise it will remain at its current value.  \\par
2.  Added SAT hysteresis cotnrol to each cycler.  the Max SAT value before the hysteresis initiated is set to 61.5 degF\\par
\\par
v75 - 5/24/23\\par
\\pard 1.\\cf0\\f0\\fs20 When the RAT dot (rate) is <= 0 AND (the algorithm goes online OR on the rising edge of a Pace ON cycle), tOn = ON TIME FRACTION * tOn previous value where ON TIME FRACTION is set to a value slightly < 1.    tOn is initialized to ON TIME IC when the pace is put online.  The RAT value is sampled when  (the algorithm goes online OR on the rising edge of a Pace ON cycle), and its previous value is maintained, RAT dot is the difference between the two values.  If RAT dot is < 0, the unit is cooling and the Pace tOn value is shortened.  Otherwise, no change is made to the Pace tOn value.  \\par
\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1 The tOff value is calculated using the same logic, however, an OFF TIME FRACTION is used and set to a value slightly >1.  Added these values to the \"Constants\" block\\par
2. increased tOnExtend from 920 to 1800 seconds to accomodate change 1. above\\par
3.  Defined new globals for RE and FE of bypass command from cloud for efficiency.removed isOnline from cycler, it is no longer used.\\par
\\cf1\\f2\\fs18\\par
v74 - 5/22/23\\par
1.  Removed all controllers except load controller and cycler\\par
2.  Bundled oem on and off time, load controller, cycler into one channel controller block, one for each of the 5 channels. \\par
3.  removed the parameter vector and all index blocks\\par
4. hardcoded to cooling mode\\par
5. Removed the delay from each cycler to prevent simulatneous compressor activation\\par
\\par
v73 - 5/15/23:\\par
1.  Removed the isbypass FE condition to generate a new RAT setpoint, now the RAT setpoint is measured at 30 min past midnight and at 8AM\\par
2.  Load Controllers:  \\par
2.1  Removed logic that provided 99999 on time from the load controller, passed isOnline to the cycler where it is used by the cycler to close the relay when isOnline is 0 and pass the pace control when isOnline is 1. \\par
2.2  Added reset of cycleValue when cloud puts the unit online from bypassed.\\par
2.3  Increased the number of oem cycles to 5 before an offline cycle is measured. \\par
2.4 added RATerror to fraction control as a linear relationship \\f0\\fs19\\par
\\pard When errorRAT = 0, onTimeFraction = OEM_FRACTION_MIN\\par
When errorRAT = 1, onTimeFraction = 1\\par
OEM_FRACTION_MIN is set = .75\\par
\\pard\\hyphpar0\\sa160\\sl252\\slmult1\\f2\\fs18\\par
3.  Cyclers:\\par
3.1  Replace tVec(4) with isOnline from load controller.  the only place tVec(4) is used is in the time based cutout, now this cutout uses tOnExtend*0.95 instead of the tVec(4) variable. \\par
3.2 Included AND uOEM to the uPace calculation to prevent cycling when uOEM is off.\\par
3.3  Added deltaTimeVecGBL = [0,10,20,30,40] second delays to ch1, ch2, ..ch5.  This delay is used in the compound block \"Time since last channel turned on\" to prevent two compressors from turning on at the same time, now they are separated by at least 10 seconds. \\par
3.4  Added a reset to the temperature cutout logic.  The logic works as follows.  If the uOEM is on for >= 30 min, then the cutout is set to 1.  The cutout is set to 0 is any of the following occur; (1) uOEM turns off, (2) uOEM on time exceeds 60 minutes, (3) cloud bypass is turned OFF (the unit is put online).  Once the cutout is reset to 0, the thermostat must cycle to fully reset it to its initial condition of detecting the OEM signal is on for more than 30 min.  \\par
4. Increased tOnMin from 4 min to 5 min \\par
\\par
V72-5/14/23:\\cf0\\f1\\fs24\\par
\\cf1\\f2\\fs18 1.  Changed the offline-online toggle behavior to 3 online cycles followed by one offline cycle to measure the OEM on and Off times.\\cf0\\f1\\fs24\\par
\\pard\\cf1\\f2\\fs18 2.  Changed the sample times for getting RAT setpoint to 30 min after midnight, 8AM, and whenever the cloud bypass is turned OFF. \\par
\\cf0\\f0\\fs20\\par
}
"
N.393="comment"*125x5*121x62
C="{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\deff0\\deflang1033{\\fonttbl{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0 Arial;}{\\f1\\froman\\fprq2\\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\\colortbl ;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;}
\\viewkind4\\uc1\\pard\\fs20 Change Log\\par
\\par
v150 - 6/24/24\\par
Identical to v149 except the Current Sensor senses current, not voltage\\par
\\par
v149 - 6/16/24 (for 2 Cypress units)\\par
1.  Apptype = 1 (cooling only, hardcoded)\\par
2.  Change current sensor to VAC Sensor\\par
3.  Corrected controller mode (correction:  0 = temperature control, 1 = time control)\\par
\\par
v148 - 3/13/24\\par
1.  Added logic to determine tOn MIN based on the AppType.  tOn MIN is used to trigger the decimation. \\par
2.  Added logic to set RAT MIN for refrigeration (37 deg) and set it to 65 deg for space cooling.\\par
3.  Fixed AppType to heatpump\\par
\\par
v147 - 3/11/24\\par
1.  Turned the extended commissioning OFF, while it was on, there were RE and FE cycles that were being counted but did not exist.  Now we will remain in commissioning until the unit naturally cycles.  NOTE:  if the unit is full on, it will never leave commissioning.  \\par
\\par
\\par
v146 - 3/3/24\\par
1.  Changed how the RAT and SAT setpoints are calculated.  They now use a continuously filters value of each measurement.  Half the peak to peak variation is added for cooling and subtracted for heating.  The overall control is the same, the difference is how the setpoint is calculated using filters instead of max and min values which do not always capture the correct setpoints.  \\par
\\par
2.  Added RAT Temp Limits to SAT and RAT Measurements.  For heating, if the RAT > RAT_MAX_LIMIT (78 deg), the internal bypass is initiated and remains bypassed until the RAT < RAT_MAX_LIMIT - 1 deg.  For cooling, if the RAT < RAT_MIN_LIMIT (60 deg), the internal bypass is initiated and remains bypassed until the RAAG > RAT_MIN_LIMIT + 1 deg.  \\par
\\par
3.  Added min On and Off Time protection to all 5 yPace output signals in Channel Controllers to prevent short cycling when the internal bypass in activated and deactivated.  The PACE_MIN_ON_TIME_SHORTCYCLE = 100 sec and PACE_MIN_OFF_TIME_SHORTCYCLE = 100 sec. \\par
\\par
v145 = v45 compiled with 2023.1\\par
Had to remove all \"limit\" blocks and replace them with Max and Min blocks.  also there were problems with undefined variables that were fixed.  \\par
\\par
v144 - 2/28/24\\par
1.  Oversized Equipment Logic:  removed the \"RE\" signal to the FF \"Set\" pin.  Also changed the \"isIncreasetOn\" logic applied to the \"Reset\" pin.  Now the \"isDecimateGBL\" signal works for heating and adjusts dynamically based on the temperature errors.\\par
2.  SAT and RAT Measurements:  Added a separate block to calculate the SAT and RAT setpoints.  Cooling Setpoints are the warmest SAT and RAT's, Heating setpoint  is the coolest RAT (SAT is not used in heating because it varies too much).    \\par
3.  v144 is hardcoded for heat pump operation\\par
\\par
v143 = v142 except is built with 2023.1 build 52\\par
1.  Codegen using 2023.1 - there was an error with ::yPace being defined in one CB and used in a second parallel level CB, this error was picked up using 2023.1 but not using 2022. This error is fixed in v143. \\par
\\par
v142 - 2/16/24\\par
1.  heating control is only based on RAT, SAT is excluded because it varies too much\\par
2.  Added logic to handle constant RAT value producing a 0 RATSetpoint, with this change the setpoint becomes RAT Max. \\par
3.  Hardcoded 142 for Apptype 6 (heat pump) \\par
\\par
v141 - 2/12/24\\par
1.  \"Heating or Cooling\" block:  Changed Heat Pump logic, if (SAT > RAT + 4deg) AND (at least one channel has been ON for 60 sec), then Mode = Heating.  if (SAT < RAT - 4 deg) AND (at least one channel has been ON for 60 sec), then Mode = Cooling.  Also added \"heatCoolModeChangeGBL\" variable which outputs a pulse when cooling changes to heating and vice versa. \\par
\\par
2.  \"Commissioning\" block:  Added \"heatCoolModeChangeGBL\" to the \"isCommishGBL\" FF.  Added \"isCommishGBL\" to the \"isOnlineAfterCommishGBL\" FF to prevent \"isOnlineAfterCommishGBL\" from being ON whick \"isCommishGBL\" is ON\\par
\\par
3.  \"SAT and RAT Measurements\" block:  SATSetpointGBL set to SATMaxCommishGBL for both heating and cooling.  Added SAT states for heating.  RATSetpointGBL set to RATMaxCommishGBL for cooling and RATMinCommishGBL for heating (cooling controls to the hottest RAT, heating controls to the coldest RAT).  Added RAT states for heating.\\par
\\par
4.  \"Temperature controller\" blocks: Added heating logic to \"Temperature States tOn\" block\\par
\\par
5.  \"Constants\" block: Added heating value for \"SAT MAX LIMIT\" (used in the RLS for SAT setpoint estimation).  Added \"isOutputVACasCurrentValue\" variable to constants, when this is set = 1, the current output is the VAC estimate (this requires the 480 VAC sensor to be attached to the CT inputs), when set = 0, cu\\cf1\\fs19\\par
\\cf0\\fs20\\par
\\cf1\\f1\\fs18 6.  Removed timer from Oversized Equipment Logic block and replaced with \"isIncreasetOn\" logic. Now \"isDecimate\" is no longer controlled by a timer, it is turned on after tOn reaches and remains on its lower limit and turns off only when the tOn command increases. \\par
\\par
7. Set the heating SAT setpoint to 100 deg instead of SATMaxCommish because there is too much variation in the SATMaxCommish signal during heating.  Using a value of 100 removes SAT control from heating.\\par
}
"
