C="{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\deff0\\deflang1033{\\fonttbl{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0 Arial;}}
\\viewkind4\\uc1\\pard\\fs18 Input = u = pace command signal raw\\par
Output = y = pace command signal\\par
\\par
This block prevents y from changing state more often than \"tOnMinGBL\" or \"TOffMinGBL\".  \\par
\\par
Logic:\\par
if u=0 && y=0 OR u=1 && y=1, then y=yPV\\par
\\par
This is the case where the raw command changes to 1 and the output is at 0, you need to wait for tOffMinGBL seconds.\\par
\\par
if u=1&&y=0&&yOffTime>=tOffMinGBL then\\par
\\tab y=u\\par
else\\par
\\tab y=yPV\\par
endif\\par
\\par
This is the case where the raw command changes to 0 and the output is at 1, you need to wait for tOnMinGBL seconds.\\par
\\par
if u=0&&y=1&&yOnTime>=tOnMinGBL then\\par
\\tab y=u\\par
else\\par
\\tab y=yPV\\par
endif\\par
\\par
NOTE:  the timers, \"yOnTime\" and \"yOffTime\" are initialized to \"tOnMinGBL\" and \"tOffMinGBL\" respectively on the first pass to the initial state change in u is captured in y.\\par
}
"
